# Milestone: M3
# Covers: '&' join of two empty blocks; result is the last expression value (2).
# blocked: `{}` is not an expression and `&` is not an expression
#          operator.  Probed: both `echo({}&{})` and `var r = {} & {}`
#          are parse errors, so the VALUE of a join of two empty blocks --
#          the entire claim -- cannot be written.
#
# Everything below this line predates the re-foundation: it names
# tasks and entry points that no longer exist, and its account of
# what stands in the way has been superseded by the `blocked:` line
# above, which was probed against this branch.  Kept for the
# original urbiscript it carries.
# matrix-row: separator-and
#
# Reason:
#   '&' (OP_FORK_JOIN / OP_JOIN_WAIT) requires the realm-managed scheduler path.
#   The chk runner uses the urbi_vm_run REPL path (realm == NULL); OP_FORK_JOIN
#   produces TypeError in that context.  See comma_amp_unsupported.chk.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5 with urbi_step chk driver):
# # {}&{};
# # 2;
# # [00000001] 2
